.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 

.PP
.nf
A wrapper iterable for dynamic ``for`` loops, with information
about the loop and iteration\&.

.fi
.PP
 
.SH "Constructor & Destructor Documentation"
.PP 
.SS " None jinja2\&.runtime\&.LoopContext\&.__init__ ( self, t\&.Iterable[\fBV\fP] iterable, t\&.Type['Undefined'] undefined, t\&.Optional['LoopRenderFunc']  recurse = \fCNone\fP, int  depth0 = \fC0\fP)"

.PP
.nf
:param iterable: Iterable to wrap\&.
:param undefined: :class:`Undefined` class to use for next and
    previous items\&.
:param recurse: The function to render the loop body when the
    loop is marked recursive\&.
:param depth0: Incremented when looping recursively\&.

.fi
.PP
 
.SH "Member Function Documentation"
.PP 
.SS " str jinja2\&.runtime\&.LoopContext\&.__call__ ( self, t\&.Iterable[\fBV\fP] iterable)"

.PP
.nf
When iterating over nested data, render the body of the loop
recursively with the given inner iterable data\&.

The loop must have the ``recursive`` marker for this to work\&.

.fi
.PP
 
